   "subject": "Re: Link to a stylesheet?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You can use the includeCSS function (which will bring it inline). Or if you&#39;re familiar with the &quot;ln&quot; Unix command, create a softlink from the css file to each &lt;appdir&gt;/www/style.css and then tags$link(rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot;, type=&quot;text/css&quot;, href=&quot;style.css&quot;)</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Jul 16, 2013 at 7:59 AM, John Lueders <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elmso...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
